{"$schema":"../gen/schemas/desktop-schema.json","description":"PACKAGING TEMPLATE — not loaded as-is (note the .template suffix). At packaging time, copy this file to remote-web.json and replace https://WEB-ORIGIN-HERE with the real production web origin (the same value as MATURIDI_WEB_URL in shell/config.js). Without this capability the production web app gets NO Tauri IPC at all: no hifz_* commands, no hifz-close-blocked event, and not even the pre-existing sync-now tray event (Tauri 2 capabilities; capabilities/default.json covers local pages only). Keep the URL list to exactly the academy origin — never '*'. The allow-hifz-* permissions are the app commands declared in src-tauri/build.rs (AppManifest::commands); keep them in sync with that list.","identifier":"remote-web","permissions":["core:default","notification:default","allow-hifz-set-recording-active","allow-hifz-is-recording-active","allow-hifz-web-base-url","allow-hifz-studio-open","allow-hifz-studio-close","allow-hifz-studio-is-open","allow-hifz-studio-layout"],"remote":{"urls":["https://WEB-ORIGIN-HERE"]},"windows":["main","hifz-practice","hifz-history"]}